error_signature: "use of undeclared identifier 'pthread_(get|set)affinity_np'|use of undeclared identifier 'RTLD_DI_ORIGIN'"
root_cause: "OHOS uses musl libc, which does not provide several glibc-only extensions. Upstream code often guards them with `#if defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(__BIONIC__)`, which is TRUE on OHOS (clang defines __linux__), so the glibc-only branch is compiled and fails: pthread_{get,set}affinity_np (glibc-only) and dlinfo(RTLD_DI_ORIGIN) (glibc extension)."
rec_approach: "Prefer the POSIX/musl-available equivalent: replace pthread_{get,set}affinity_np with sched_{get,set}affinity(0, ...) (musl provides the cpu_set_t + CPU_* macros and sched_*affinity in <sched.h>). For APIs with no equivalent, guard with `#if defined(__GLIBC__)` (affinity) or `#if defined(RTLD_DI_ORIGIN)` (dlinfo) so musl skips the block. Do NOT rely on `defined(__linux__)` to mean glibc."
match_keywords: ["pthread_getaffinity_np", "pthread_setaffinity_np", "RTLD_DI_ORIGIN", "dlinfo", "musl", "glibc", "__OHOS__", "__BIONIC__", "sched_setaffinity"]
error_excerpt: "third_party/marl/src/thread.cpp:161:7: error: use of undeclared identifier 'pthread_getaffinity_np'  ;  tests/VulkanWrapper/VulkanTester.cpp:236:16: error: use of undeclared identifier 'RTLD_DI_ORIGIN'"
severity: P1
category: platform
last_updated: 2026-09-30
